      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To maintain a strict cold chain during international transport of mRNA vaccines, check the following:\n\n* Verify all shipments are packaged inapproved protective devices, including vials, trays, or boxes, and are specifically designed to maintain a temperature range of -80°C to -15°C.\n* Ensure each shipment is labeled with its temperature requirement, handling instructions, and any relevant cold chain documentation.\n* Conduct regular temperature checks at both the export and import locations, as well as during transit, to monitor temperature excursions and correct them promptly if necessary.\n* Maintain accurate records of all temperature checks, shipping passes, and cold chain documentation for at least 24 months.",
